Jay Finechem Private Limited shall evaluate environmentally preferable alternatives during the selection and approval of new raw materials and significant changes to existing raw materials.
Where technically and commercially feasible, the evaluation shall consider:
Bio-based or renewable content;
Recycled or recovered content;
Hazard classification;
Toxicity;
Biodegradability;
VOC content;
Resource efficiency;
Environmental impact;
Product and process performance;
Regulatory requirements; and
Supply availability and reliability.
Where an eco-friendly, bio-based, renewable, recycled, or otherwise environmentally preferable material can provide equivalent or acceptable technical performance, the alternative shall be evaluated for approval.
The Procurement, R&D, Production, and EHS functions shall participate in the evaluation as applicable.
The basis for approving or rejecting an environmentally preferable alternative shall be documented.

Jay Finechem Private Limited shall prioritize authorized domestic treatment, recycling, recovery, and disposal routes for hazardous waste generated from its operations.
Routine transboundary movement of hazardous waste shall not be undertaken where an appropriate authorized domestic treatment, recycling, recovery, or disposal facility is available.
Where transboundary movement of hazardous waste is proposed or becomes necessary, the movement shall be subject to prior review and approval by the responsible EHS and management personnel.
Before any transboundary movement is authorized, the following shall be verified:
Waste classification and characteristics;
Applicable national and international legal requirements;
Required regulatory permissions, approvals, and notifications;
Authorization of the transporter;
Authorization and suitability of the receiving facility;
Required manifests and shipment documentation;
Appropriate packaging, labelling, and transportation controls; and
Confirmation of receipt and final treatment or disposal.
No hazardous waste shall be transferred to an unapproved or unauthorized destination.
The EHS function shall maintain records of any approved hazardous waste movement, including waste type, quantity, transporter, destination, regulatory approvals, manifests, and final treatment or disposal documentation.
Where domestic authorized treatment or disposal is available, the domestic route shall be prioritized to minimize unnecessary cross-border movement of hazardous waste.

