For applicable products, Jay Finechem Private Limited shall evaluate opportunities to reduce product dosage, quantity, or application frequency while maintaining the required product performance and intended application outcome.
The R&D function shall use appropriate technical evaluation methods, which may include:
Laboratory trials;
Pilot-scale testing;
Field trials;
Comparative performance testing;
Formulation optimization;
Controlled-release studies; and
Other suitable technical validation methods.
Where a reduction in dosage, quantity, or application frequency is technically validated, the results shall be documented and incorporated into the applicable product specification, technical guidance, or customer-use recommendation.
The evaluation shall compare the previous and optimized application requirements and document the corresponding product-performance results.
No reduction in recommended dosage or application frequency shall be adopted without appropriate technical validation.

Jay Finechem Private Limited shall conduct environmental impact assessments for selected products, particularly new products, significantly reformulated products, and products identified as having significant environmental impacts.
The assessment shall consider relevant lifecycle stages, as applicable:
Raw material selection;
Raw material consumption;
Manufacturing processes;
Energy consumption;
Water consumption;
Greenhouse gas emissions;
Chemical toxicity;
Effluent and emissions;
Product-use impacts;
Packaging;
Transportation; and
Product and packaging end-of-life.
The assessment shall identify significant environmental impact areas or hotspots and evaluate technically feasible improvement opportunities.
Where significant environmental impacts are identified, the R&D, Production, EHS, Procurement, and other relevant functions shall evaluate appropriate improvement measures.
The findings, identified hotspots, improvement actions, and follow-up assessment results shall be documented as part of the product development or reformulation process.

For new products and significant formulation changes, Jay Finechem Private Limited shall evaluate the potential for product constituents, residues, or degradation products to contribute to toxic environmental discharges during product use or subsequent handling.
The review shall consider, where applicable:
Aquatic toxicity;
Biodegradability;
Persistence;
Bioaccumulation potential;
Hazardous functional groups;
Heavy metals;
Persistent organic pollutants;
Restricted substances;
Toxic residues; and
Potential impacts on wastewater or receiving environments.
Where an environmental concern is identified, R&D and EHS shall evaluate technically feasible formulation improvements, including:
Substitution of higher-risk ingredients;
Reduction of hazardous constituents;
Use of biodegradable alternatives;
Formulation optimization;
Controlled-release approaches; and
Other measures that reduce potential environmental toxicity.
The final assessment and formulation decision shall be documented and approved through the applicable product-development or reformulation process.
